<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Queen Victoria is proclaimed Empress of India at the Delhi Durbar</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Buganda.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Buganda</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Protestant missionaries arrive in Buganda</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/south-african-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/South%20African%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>South African Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain annexes the bankrupt republic</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/rapa-nui"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rapa%20Nui.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rapa Nui</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The island’s population falls to 111</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/jomon-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/J%C5%8Dmon%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jōmon culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Edward S. Morse finds cord-marked sherds and gives the culture its name</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/lili-uokalani"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lili%CA%BBuokalani.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liliʻuokalani</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the death of her brother Leleiohoku she is designated heir apparent on 10 April and given the name Liliʻuokalani by King Kalākaua</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/frederick-douglass"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Frederick%20Douglass.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Frederick Douglass</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Becomes United States Marshal for the District of Columbia, the first person of colour named to the post</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/pali-canon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pali%20Canon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pali Canon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Pali Text Society begins to publish its edition in Roman script, completed in 1927</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/guru-granth-sahib"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Guru%20Granth%20Sahib.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Guru Granth Sahib</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Ernest Trumpp publishes the first philological study and a major but incomplete English translation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-little-bighorn"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Little%20Bighorn.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Little Bighorn</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sitting Bull escapes to Canada, Crazy Horse surrenders and the Great Sioux War ends</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/sitting-bull"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sitting%20Bull.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sitting Bull</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">He leads his band across the border to Wood Mountain in the North-West Territories</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/rabindranath-tagore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Rabindranath%20Tagore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Rabindranath Tagore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Presents poems as the lost works of a 17th-century poet, Bhanusimha, and debuts in the short story with &quot;Bhikharini&quot;</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/social-darwinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Social%20Darwinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Social Darwinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The phrase social Darwinism first appears in print, in Joseph Fisher's article on landholding in Ireland, and Eduard Oscar Schmidt uses it at a conference in Munich</span></li></ul></section>
